1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,194
This is one woman, photographed once,
wearing the same garment in two colors.

2
00:00:04,194 --> 00:00:06,209
Watch her face rather than the shirt.

3
00:00:06,659 --> 00:00:11,358
Some colors suit you and some drain you,
and most people never find out which.

4
00:00:11,358 --> 00:00:15,576
A stylist will tell you for a hundred and
fifty dollars. This is Drape.

5
00:00:15,576 --> 00:00:20,095
It answers the same question from one
photo, in about twenty seconds, free.

6
00:00:20,545 --> 00:00:21,818
You give it a selfie.

7
00:00:21,818 --> 00:00:26,304
Perfect Corp's YouCam API measures the
real color of your skin, your eyes,

8
00:00:26,304 --> 00:00:29,214
your lips and your hair, straight off the
image.

9
00:00:29,664 --> 00:00:33,890
Our engine turns those measurements into
your season. There are twelve,

10
00:00:33,890 --> 00:00:38,418
and each carries about a dozen shades
chosen to sit well against your face.

11
00:00:38,868 --> 00:00:40,535
Here is what most tools skip.

12
00:00:40,535 --> 00:00:42,317
Drape tells you how sure it is.

13
00:00:42,767 --> 00:00:46,797
This read scores forty-one out of a
hundred, and it says why in one line.

14
00:00:46,797 --> 00:00:51,213
Her depth measurement came in one point
four from the boundary between light and

15
00:00:51,213 --> 00:00:54,525
medium. That close, it could go either
way, so Drape says so.

16
00:00:54,975 --> 00:00:57,721
And if you think it has read you wrong,
you can overrule it.

17
00:00:58,171 --> 00:01:01,962
Tap depth, choose medium, and the whole
result recalculates in your browser.

18
00:01:01,962 --> 00:01:03,608
Confidence climbs to eighty-four,

19
00:01:03,608 --> 00:01:06,801
because you have just settled the one
thing it was unsure about.

20
00:01:06,801 --> 00:01:08,847
That correction is free and calls no API.

21
00:01:09,297 --> 00:01:11,029
Then it proves the answer on you.

22
00:01:11,029 --> 00:01:14,282
YouCam's virtual try-on paints the colors
onto your own photo.

23
00:01:14,282 --> 00:01:15,752
One shade from your palette,

24
00:01:15,752 --> 00:01:18,743
and one taken deliberately from the
opposite temperature.

25
00:01:19,193 --> 00:01:21,158
Same garment, same face, same light.

26
00:01:21,158 --> 00:01:23,287
The color is the only thing that moved.

27
00:01:23,737 --> 00:01:26,147
A palette you cannot buy is a piece of
trivia.

28
00:01:26,597 --> 00:01:30,916
So Drape ranks three hundred and
fifty-three real garments you can order to

29
00:01:30,916 --> 00:01:32,829
We did not trust the product names.

30
00:01:32,829 --> 00:01:36,983
Every one of those colors was measured
from the retailer's own fabric photo.

31
00:01:37,433 --> 00:01:39,611
This top match scores four point five.

32
00:01:39,611 --> 00:01:44,026
Below about two point three, most people
cannot tell two colors apart at all,

33
00:01:44,026 --> 00:01:46,491
so on a shop floor this reads as her
shade.

34
00:01:46,941 --> 00:01:51,516
More in the studio. Your own hair color,
held against the shades your season wears.

35
00:01:51,516 --> 00:01:54,138
Eleven skin scores from YouCam's skin
analysis.

36
00:01:54,588 --> 00:01:56,806
And you can ask it for a whole outfit.

37
00:01:56,806 --> 00:02:01,124
This one is generative rather than
measured, so give it a moment to think.

38
00:02:01,574 --> 00:02:04,937
Clothes, styling and setting, all built
around True Spring.

39
00:02:04,937 --> 00:02:07,786
Inspiration, where the palette is the
measurement.

40
00:02:08,236 --> 00:02:10,525
Now the part we are least comfortable
with.

41
00:02:10,525 --> 00:02:12,760
Color analysis was built around pale skin,

42
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:17,125
so we tested our own engine against the
Monk Skin Tone Scale, ten reference tones,

43
00:02:17,125 --> 00:02:20,211
and we failed. Our rule was reading dark
skin as cool skin.

44
00:02:20,211 --> 00:02:23,405
It got five of the ten wrong, all at the
light or deep ends.

45
00:02:23,855 --> 00:02:26,168
So we rebuilt it on a different
measurement,

46
00:02:26,168 --> 00:02:29,007
and we published the before and the after
on the site.

47
00:02:29,007 --> 00:02:31,793
You can check our working instead of
taking our word.

48
00:02:32,243 --> 00:02:36,021
Underneath: five YouCam APIs, two hundred
and seven tests,

49
00:02:36,021 --> 00:02:39,539
and the whole color engine open to AI
agents over MCP.

50
00:02:39,989 --> 00:02:44,374
Drape. One photo, the colors that suit
you, worn on your own face,

51
00:02:44,374 --> 00:02:46,601
and clothes you can actually buy.
